  "term": "trifluoperazine",
  "definition": "Trifluoperazine is a phenothiazine drug that blocks dopamine receptors in the brain, giving it antipsychotic effects and helping reduce symptoms such as delusions and hallucinations linked to excess dopamine. It also has antiemetic activity and can inhibit calmodulin, which raises calcium levels within cells.",
